<title>UK: Pepsi up in London on food spin-off talk.</title>
<headline>Pepsi up in London on food spin-off talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in PepsiCo Inc were higher in Europe on Thursday following press reports that the company is on the verge of spinning off its $11 billion restaurant business, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Wall Street Journal reported that Pepsi's board was scheduled to meet on Thursday and could make an announcement about the spin-off later today.</p>
<p>&quot;Talk of spin-off of the foods business has been around for quite awhile,&quot; one market maker said. &quot;But some people think that a deal may have been done.&quot;</p>
<p>Pepsi was trading at $33-1/2 versus $31-7/8 in New York.</p>
<p>Pepsi's restaurant division includes the Pizza Hut, Kentucky Fried Chicken and Taco Bell fast-food chains.</p>
<p>-- Dale Faulken, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
